// Service diagnostics (ridl §14.5, §16.4): RIDL-142 for a service named in the
// old dotted form, RIDL-141, and the composition rules RIDL-144 and RIDL-145.

package diag.ridl

interface Published {
  signal speed : Speed @10ms
}

/// A service declared with a dotted name (RIDL-142). It binds nothing, and the
/// diagnostic suggests `ShowcaseLegacy`.
service diag.showcase.legacy : Published

/// `Sample` is a struct, not an interface, and no inline shape is given.
service Mistyped : Sample

/// Both declare `status`, so `diag.ridl.Doors.status` would have two
/// referents (RIDL-144) — flat addressing cannot express that.
interface DoorBlock {
  signal status : Speed @10ms
}

interface HealthBlock {
  signal status : Speed @10ms
}

service Doors : DoorBlock, HealthBlock

/// The same interface listed twice (RIDL-145) — its own code, so the mistake
/// is one diagnostic rather than one RIDL-144 per member.
service Twice : Published, Published
